schema: design.v1
name: wx-channels-download
version: 1.0.0
status: bootstrap
updated_at: 2026-09-12
description: Living visual contract extracted from the frontend DMUI token and page-composition layers.

agent:
  skill: design
  instructions: |
    This file is the visual source of truth for the wx_channels_download frontend.
    If the AgentsORG `design` skill is installed, activate it and still treat this
    contract as normative.

    READ
    - Read intent, constraints, policy, decisions, tokens, themes, voice,
      components, patterns, sources, and locked before changing UI.
    - `frontend/src/dmui.css` is the implementation source for design tokens and
      reusable DMUI components. `frontend/src/style.css` is the implementation
      source for shared page composition.

    FOLLOW
    - Match the existing Timeless/DMUI component stack; do not introduce a
      parallel styling framework.
    - Reuse a catalogued component or the nearest approved variant before adding
      a page-specific primitive.
    - Consume `--dm-*` semantic CSS variables. Do not copy palette values into
      page styles or JavaScript.
    - Apply the active light, explicit-dark, or system-dark theme without
      component-level theme overrides.
    - Keep the product utilitarian and dense. Spend visual emphasis on the
      Folder Gold primary action and selected state, not decoration.
    - Preserve keyboard focus, disabled, loading, empty, error, hover, active,
      and selected states when the component supports them.

    UPDATE
    - Edit this file in place when the design system changes and bump SemVer.
    - Ask before changing a path listed in `locked`. Git is the history.
    - Keep the CSS implementation and this contract synchronized in the same
      change when tokens or catalogued components change.

    VERIFY
    - Compare tokens against `frontend/src/dmui.css` and shared patterns against
      `frontend/src/style.css`.
    - Report token and component drift as added, removed, or modified, and mark
      whether the drift is a consumer regression.
    - Verify both light and dark mappings, visible focus, responsive states, and
      `prefers-reduced-motion` handling. Never automate a browser in this repo;
      finish with static checks and leave browser verification to the user.

    PRECEDENCE
    1. Current user request
    2. This contract
    3. The design skill
    4. Generic UI conventions

overview: |
  A compact desktop workbench with the visual memory of file folders, warm
  paper, and archive labels. Modern application chrome keeps the interface
  operational rather than nostalgic: shallow surfaces, crisp separators,
  squared four-pixel corners, dense data rows, and direct controls. Warm neutral
  layers reduce glare while Folder Gold makes the single primary action and
  selected state immediately recognizable.

intent:
  reference: "A Folder Gold desktop workbench: warm paper and archive-label tactility expressed through compact modern application chrome."
  direction: warm-archival-workbench
  signature: "Folder Gold fill and a narrow gold selection indicator reserved for the primary action, active tab, and current item."
  treatment: utilitarian
  density: compact
  trust: high
  character: warm, practical, precise

voice:
  language: zh-CN
  register: "Direct, calm, and task-oriented; friendly without being playful."
  casing: sentence
  terminology:
    preserve:
      - Pipeline
      - ID
      - URL
      - JSON
    preferred:
      automation: 自动化
      refresh: 刷新
      create: 创建
      save: 保存
      delete: 删除
      cancel: 取消
  actions: "Use a verb plus the concrete object, such as ‘创建 Pipeline’ or ‘保存设置’."
  empty_states: "State what is absent and name the next useful action."
  loading: "Name the object being loaded; use an ellipsis character when progress is ongoing."
  success: "Confirm the completed action and mention the next step only when it is useful."
  errors: "Say which action failed, include the useful cause when known, and provide a recovery step."
  destructive: "Use explicit object names; do not disguise destructive actions behind vague labels."

tokens:
  color:
    canvas: "#f3f2ee"
    surface: "#fffefa"
    surface-subtle: "#f8f5ec"
    surface-interactive: "#eee8d9"
    popup: "#fffaf0"
    inverse: "#292317"
    inverse-hover: "#3a301d"
    text-primary: "#29251d"
    text-secondary: "#706958"
    text-disabled: "#a39a87"
    text-inverse: "#fff9eb"
    text-inverse-secondary: "#cfc2a5"
    border: "#e2dccf"
    border-strong: "#c9bfaa"
    border-translucent: "rgba(41, 37, 29, 0.13)"
    fill-translucent: "rgba(41, 37, 29, 0.06)"
    primary-text: "#9a5800"
    primary-text-hover: "#754200"
    primary-fill: "#f3b41b"
    primary-fill-hover: "#d99a00"
    on-primary: "#2d1b00"
    primary-soft: "#fff1c7"
    primary-border: "rgba(183, 112, 0, 0.30)"
    primary-border-strong: "rgba(154, 88, 0, 0.58)"
    signal: "#ffbf2f"
    signal-soft: "rgba(255, 191, 47, 0.18)"
    signal-glow: "rgba(243, 180, 27, 0.34)"
    success: "#178353"
    success-soft: "#e2f5e9"
    warning: "#b34f00"
    warning-soft: "#fff0df"
    danger: "#c84646"
    danger-soft: "#fdeeee"
    danger-border: "rgba(200, 70, 70, 0.34)"
    info: "#286f9f"
    info-soft: "#e8f3fa"
    info-border: "rgba(40, 111, 159, 0.30)"
    accent-violet: "#7256b8"
    accent-violet-soft: "rgba(114, 86, 184, 0.12)"
    accent-sky: "#187da1"
    accent-sky-soft: "rgba(24, 125, 161, 0.12)"
    accent-amber: "#a7660d"
    accent-amber-soft: "rgba(167, 102, 13, 0.13)"
    sidebar-border: "rgba(255, 225, 153, 0.12)"
    focus-ring: "rgba(243, 180, 27, 0.30)"
    scrim: "rgba(24, 18, 7, 0.82)"
    skeleton: "rgba(41, 37, 29, 0.08)"
    skeleton-highlight: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.62)"
    chart-grid: "rgba(112, 95, 63, 0.20)"
    disabled-fill: "#cbc3b3"
    scrollbar: "rgba(41, 37, 29, 0.20)"
    scrollbar-hover: "rgba(41, 37, 29, 0.38)"
    media-canvas: "#090804"
    media-surface: "rgba(25, 22, 14, 0.92)"
    media-surface-hover: "rgba(42, 36, 21, 0.94)"
    media-text: "#fffaf0"
    media-muted: "#bdb4a2"
    media-border: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.20)"
    document-canvas: "#ffffff"
    selection:
      surface: "{tokens.color.primary-soft}"
      surface-hover: "color-mix(in srgb, var(--dm-color-primary-soft) 90%, var(--dm-color-primary-fill))"
      border: "{tokens.color.primary-border-strong}"
      text: "{tokens.color.primary-text}"
      indicator: "{tokens.color.primary-fill}"
      indicator-text: "{tokens.color.on-primary}"
      halo: "{tokens.color.signal-soft}"

  typography:
    family:
      display: 'Bahnschrift, "DIN Alternate", "Segoe UI Variable Display", "PingFang SC", "Microsoft YaHei", sans-serif'
      sans: '"Segoe UI Variable Text", Aptos, "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans GB", "Microsoft YaHei", system-ui, sans-serif'
      mono: '"Cascadia Mono", "SFMono-Regular", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace'
    size:
      caption-compact: 10px
      xs: 11px
      sm: 12px
      md: 13px
      base: 14px
      ui: 15px
      lg: 16px
      heading-sm: 17px
      xl: 18px
      heading-md: 20px
      2xl: 21px
      3xl: 24px
      display: 40px
    weight:
      regular: 400
      medium: 500
      semibold: 600
      bold: 700
    line-height:
      tight: 1.2
      snug: 1.35
      base: 1.5
      relaxed: 1.7
    letter-spacing:
      tight: -0.02em
      normal: 0
      wide: 0.08em
    roles:
      page-title:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.display}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.3xl}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.semibold}"
        lineHeight: "{tokens.typography.line-height.tight}"
        letterSpacing: "{tokens.typography.letter-spacing.tight}"
      section-title:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.display}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.lg}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.bold}"
        lineHeight: "{tokens.typography.line-height.tight}"
      body:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.sans}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.base}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.regular}"
        lineHeight: "{tokens.typography.line-height.base}"
      control:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.sans}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.md}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.semibold}"
        lineHeight: 1
      caption:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.sans}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.sm}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.regular}"
        lineHeight: "{tokens.typography.line-height.base}"
      code:
        fontFamily: "{tokens.typography.family.mono}"
        fontSize: "{tokens.typography.size.sm}"
        fontWeight: "{tokens.typography.weight.regular}"
        lineHeight: "{tokens.typography.line-height.relaxed}"

  spacing:
    unit: 4px
    0: 0
    0-5: 2px
    1: 4px
    1-5: 6px
    2: 8px
    2-5: 10px
    3: 12px
    3-5: 14px
    4: 16px
    4-5: 18px
    5: 20px
    6: 24px
    7: 28px
    8: 32px
    9: 36px
    10: 40px
    12: 48px
    16: 64px
    24: 96px

  border:
    default: 1px
    strong: 2px

  radius:
    none: 0
    xs: 4px
    sm: 6px
    md: 8px
    lg: 12px
    xl: 16px
    2xl: 20px
    full: 9999px
    control: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
    content: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
    card: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
    overlay: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
    badge: "{tokens.radius.xs}"
    avatar: "{tokens.radius.xs}"

  size:
    control:
      xs: 28px
      sm: 32px
      md: 38px
      base: 40px
      lg: 44px
      textarea-min-height: 96px
    layout:
      min-width: 320px
      sidebar-width: 248px
      content-max: 1320px
      popover-width: 288px
      dropdown-min-width: 160px
      dialog-width: 640px

  motion:
    fast: 120ms
    base: 160ms
    slow: 240ms
    loop: 800ms
    easing-standard: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1)
    easing-emphasized: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1.2)
    route-enter: "Fade and translate 24px from the inline end with a 0.985 scale."
    route-exit: "Fade and translate 12px toward the inline start with a 0.995 scale."
    overlay-enter: "Fade; dialogs also translate 8px and scale from 0.98."
    reduced: "Remove spatial route, overlay, navigation, shimmer, and branded loading motion while preserving state clarity."

  opacity:
    disabled: 0.72

  z-index:
    base: 0
    raised: 2
    sticky: 20
    overlay: 50
    dropdown: 1000

  elevation:
    sm: "0 1px 2px rgba(77, 57, 18, 0.08)"
    md: "0 12px 30px rgba(77, 57, 18, 0.12)"
    lg: "0 24px 64px rgba(77, 57, 18, 0.17)"
    popover: "0 12px 36px rgba(77, 57, 18, 0.21)"
    divider: "0 1px 0 rgba(77, 57, 18, 0.10)"
    selection: "inset 3px 0 0 var(--dm-color-primary-fill), 0 6px 18px var(--dm-color-signal-soft)"
    focus: "0 0 0 3px var(--dm-color-focus-ring)"

  sound:
    enabled: false
    material: none

themes:
  default: light
  modes:
    light:
      selector: ":root, body[data-weui-theme='light']"
      description: "Warm parchment canvas, ivory surfaces, umber text, and saturated Folder Gold controls."
    dark:
      selector: ".dark, body[data-weui-theme='dark']"
      description: "Layered charcoal-brown surfaces with desaturated warm borders and luminous gold text accents."
      tokens:
        color:
          canvas: "#17150f"
          surface: "#201d16"
          surface-subtle: "#2b271d"
          surface-interactive: "#373020"
          popup: "#1c1912"
          inverse: "#13110c"
          inverse-hover: "#332b19"
          text-primary: "#f8f3e7"
          text-secondary: "#bbb19e"
          text-disabled: "#827967"
          text-inverse: "#fff8e8"
          text-inverse-secondary: "#bbaa86"
          border: "#413b2f"
          border-strong: "#5d5340"
          border-translucent: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10)"
          fill-translucent: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)"
          primary-text: "#ffd166"
          primary-text-hover: "#ffe09a"
          primary-fill: "#f2ad18"
          primary-fill-hover: "#ffc43d"
          on-primary: "#281800"
          primary-soft: "rgba(255, 191, 47, 0.16)"
          primary-border: "rgba(255, 209, 102, 0.30)"
          primary-border-strong: "rgba(255, 209, 102, 0.64)"
          signal: "#ffc43d"
          signal-soft: "rgba(255, 196, 61, 0.17)"
          signal-glow: "rgba(255, 196, 61, 0.34)"
          success: "#63dda0"
          success-soft: "rgba(99, 221, 160, 0.13)"
          warning: "#ff9855"
          warning-soft: "rgba(255, 152, 85, 0.14)"
          danger: "#ff8585"
          danger-soft: "rgba(255, 133, 133, 0.13)"
          danger-border: "rgba(255, 133, 133, 0.42)"
          info: "#74b9e8"
          info-soft: "rgba(116, 185, 232, 0.14)"
          info-border: "rgba(116, 185, 232, 0.34)"
          accent-violet: "#b09ae8"
          accent-violet-soft: "rgba(176, 154, 232, 0.14)"
          accent-sky: "#6fc6e5"
          accent-sky-soft: "rgba(111, 198, 229, 0.14)"
          accent-amber: "#e8ae58"
          accent-amber-soft: "rgba(232, 174, 88, 0.14)"
          sidebar-border: "rgba(255, 222, 141, 0.10)"
          focus-ring: "rgba(255, 196, 61, 0.30)"
          skeleton: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.10)"
          skeleton-highlight: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.16)"
          chart-grid: "rgba(187, 177, 158, 0.22)"
          disabled-fill: "#514a3d"
          scrollbar: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.20)"
          scrollbar-hover: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.36)"
          media-canvas: "#080703"
          media-surface: "rgba(20, 17, 10, 0.94)"
          media-surface-hover: "rgba(51, 43, 25, 0.96)"
          media-text: "#fff8e8"
          media-muted: "#b9ae98"
          media-border: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.18)"
        elevation:
          sm: "0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.30)"
          md: "0 14px 34px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.38)"
          lg: "0 24px 64px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.46)"
          popover: "0 14px 40px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.50)"
          divider: "0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06)"
    system-dark:
      media: "(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"
      when: "body:not([data-weui-theme='light'])"
      inherits: dark

components:
  button:
    implementation: ".dm-button"
    when: ["A labeled action or icon action"]
    when_not: ["Navigation rows with application-specific structure", "A non-interactive status"]
    variants: [default, primary, secondary, outline, surface, ghost, link, danger, icon, toolbar, list-row, choice-card, disclosure, media]
    states: [default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, loading, selected]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface-interactive}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.3-5}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: auto
      primary:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.primary-fill}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.on-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.3-5}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: auto
      ghost:
        backgroundColor: transparent
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.3-5}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: auto

  field:
    implementation: ".dm-field, .dm-input-affix-wrapper, .dm-textarea, .dm-select"
    when: ["Text, structured data, or selection input"]
    when_not: ["Read-only metadata that should be plain text"]
    states: [default, hover, focus-within, disabled, invalid, loading]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface-subtle}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.body}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.3}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: 100%

  tabs:
    implementation: ".dm-tabs, .dm-tab"
    when: ["Peer views or status filters inside one page context"]
    when_not: ["Primary application navigation", "A sequential wizard"]
    states: [default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled]
    tokens:
      container:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface-subtle}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-secondary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.content}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.1}"
        height: 42px
        width: auto
      active:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.primary-fill}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.on-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.3}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.sm}"
        width: auto

  tag:
    implementation: ".dm-tag"
    when: ["Compact category, source, or status metadata"]
    when_not: ["An actionable filter without button semantics"]
    variants: [neutral, success, warning, danger, info]
    tokens:
      neutral:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface-interactive}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-secondary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.badge}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.2}"
        height: "{tokens.spacing.5}"
        width: auto

  panel:
    implementation: ".dm-panel, .dm-card, .dm-list-card"
    when: ["A grouped content surface requiring separation from the canvas"]
    when_not: ["Every row in a dense list when separators are sufficient"]
    variants: [default, soft, card, list-card, choice-card]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.body}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.card}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.5}"
        height: auto
        width: 100%

  overlay:
    implementation: ".dm-dialog-content, .dm-drawer-content, .dm-popover-content, .dm-dropdown-content, .dm-select-content"
    when: ["Focused blocking tasks or contextual floating controls"]
    when_not: ["Information that belongs in the normal page flow"]
    variants: [dialog, drawer, popover, dropdown, select]
    states: [entering, open, exiting]
    tokens:
      dialog:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.body}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.overlay}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.5}"
        height: auto
        width: "{tokens.size.layout.dialog-width}"
      popover:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.overlay}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.3}"
        height: auto
        width: "{tokens.size.layout.popover-width}"

  alert:
    implementation: ".dm-alert"
    when: ["Persistent inline notice, request error, or important state"]
    when_not: ["Brief success confirmation that does not need to remain in layout"]
    variants: [default, destructive]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.content}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.4}"
        height: auto
        width: 100%
      destructive:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.danger-soft}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.danger}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.content}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.4}"
        height: auto
        width: 100%

  checkbox:
    implementation: ".dm-checkbox, .dm-checkbox-box, .dm-checkbox-text"
    when: ["Independent boolean settings or multi-selection"]
    when_not: ["A single mutually exclusive choice; use radio or choice-card semantics"]
    states: [default, hover, focus-visible, checked, indeterminate, disabled]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: transparent
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-secondary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: 0
        height: 22px
        width: 22px
      checked:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.primary-fill}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.on-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.caption}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: 0
        height: 22px
        width: 22px

  navigation-item:
    implementation: ".dm-button--sidebar-nav"
    when: ["Primary application route navigation"]
    when_not: ["Peer tabs within one route"]
    states: [default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: transparent
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-secondary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.2} {tokens.spacing.2-5}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: 100%
      active:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.primary-soft}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.primary-text}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.control}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.2} {tokens.spacing.2-5}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.md}"
        width: 100%

  state:
    implementation: ".dm-empty-state, .dm-table-state, .content-state, .route-error-card"
    when: ["Loading, empty, error, or no-selection state replacing a content region"]
    when_not: ["Transient progress inside a single button"]
    variants: [loading, empty, error, no-selection]
    tokens:
      default:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-secondary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.body}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.content}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.8}"
        height: 320px
        width: 100%

  data-table:
    implementation: ".dm-table-panel, .dm-table-header, .dm-table-row, .dm-table-cell"
    when: ["Comparable records with stable columns and dense scanning"]
    when_not: ["Heterogeneous content better represented by cards"]
    states: [default, striped, loading, empty, error]
    tokens:
      row:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.body}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.none}"
        padding: "{tokens.spacing.2} {tokens.spacing.3}"
        height: 72px
        width: 100%

  pagination:
    implementation: ".dm-pagination, .dm-pagination__page, .dm-pagination__button"
    when: ["A bounded dataset split into numbered pages"]
    when_not: ["Continuous discovery feeds; use an explicit load-more or virtualized pattern"]
    states: [default, hover, active, focus-visible, disabled, loading]
    tokens:
      page:
        backgroundColor: "{tokens.color.surface}"
        textColor: "{tokens.color.text-primary}"
        typography: "{tokens.typography.roles.code}"
        rounded: "{tokens.radius.control}"
        padding: "0 {tokens.spacing.2}"
        height: "{tokens.size.control.sm}"
        width: "{tokens.size.control.sm}"

patterns:
  application-shell:
    treatment: utilitarian
    use: "Persistent application navigation around one scroll-contained route view."
    composition: "Sidebar or compact mobile navigation + route content + tokenized canvas."
    rules:
      - Keep global navigation visually quieter than the active workspace.
      - Use the shared z-index scale for sticky and overlay layers.
      - At 640px, collapse navigation into compact 44px-minimum touch targets.

  content-page:
    treatment: utilitarian
    use: "Standard data-management and settings pages."
    composition: "Optional sticky header + toolbar + flexible content-main."
    rules:
      - Toolbar places context and peer navigation first; actions align at the inline end.
      - Use one filled primary action; refresh, filters, and secondary actions use outline or ghost variants.
      - Shared horizontal page padding is 16px on compact layouts and may expand to 32px on wide headers.
      - Let the content region, not the document body, own overflow for application-height pages.

  master-detail:
    treatment: utilitarian
    use: "Selectable pipelines, schedules, accounts, or other records with an adjacent editor/detail."
    composition: "Bounded list rail + flexible detail region; stack when content no longer fits."
    rules:
      - Selected items use the selection surface, border, and narrow indicator.
      - Keep list titles single-line with an accessible route to the full value.
      - Preserve loading, empty, no-selection, and stale-selection states.

  data-management:
    treatment: utilitarian
    use: "Filterable, paginated record collections."
    composition: "Toolbar/filter form + bounded table/list + pagination."
    rules:
      - Reserve space for asynchronous rows and pagination controls.
      - Use tabular numerals for counts, pages, timestamps, and stable numeric columns.
      - At 760px wrap toolbars; at 520px stack filters and allow actions to share the row width.

  form-dialog:
    treatment: utilitarian
    use: "Short creation or editing task that should preserve page context."
    composition: "Title/description + scrollable body + separated footer actions."
    rules:
      - Place the primary commit action at the footer inline end and disable it while submitting.
      - Use explicit labels and inline validation; retain entered values after recoverable errors.
      - Use the scrim, overlay elevation, focus containment, Escape/outside dismissal when safe, and focus return.

decisions:
  action-emphasis:
    - if: "The action is the single primary completion action for the current view or dialog."
      then: "Use components.button primary."
    - if: "The action is refresh, cancel, browse, filter, or another supporting action."
      then: "Use outline, surface, or ghost according to surrounding separation."
    - if: "The action is destructive."
      then: "Use the danger treatment, name the target, separate it from confirmation, and require explicit confirmation for irreversible work."

  surface-choice:
    - if: "A region needs elevation above the page or blocks the current task."
      then: "Use an overlay with popover elevation and the appropriate scrim."
    - if: "A region only needs grouping or row separation."
      then: "Use a panel/card or a border separator; do not add decorative elevation."

  selection:
    - if: "A row, card, tab, or compact option represents the current item."
      then: "Use the Folder Gold selection surface, border, and indicator; never rely on color alone when an indicator or label can be present."

  missing-component:
    - if: "A requested UI has no exact catalog entry."
      then: "Adapt the nearest DMUI primitive, keep semantic tokens, document the new reusable variant here if it appears in more than one feature."

policy:
  if_missing: nearest
  hierarchy: [typography, spacing, contrast, color]
  reuse:
    order: [existing-page-pattern, catalogued-DMUI-component, nearest-DMUI-variant, new-reusable-variant]
    page_specific: "Only business structure and content-derived geometry belong in page CSS."
  color:
    accent_cycle: [primary-fill, accent-sky, accent-violet, accent-amber]
    semantic: "Gold is brand/action/selection; green is success; orange is warning; red is danger; blue is information."
  accessibility:
    contrast: "Target WCAG AA: 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for large text and essential UI boundaries."
    focus: "Every keyboard-interactive control has a visible focus ring using the shared focus token."
    input_labels: "Inputs have programmatic labels; placeholder text is supporting copy, not the label."
    targets: "Prefer 40px desktop and 44px touch targets; smaller visible controls require a non-overlapping enlarged hit area."
    motion: "Honor prefers-reduced-motion and never make motion the only state signal."
    color_only: "Error, selection, and status must include text, icon, border, or shape in addition to color."
  responsive:
    breakpoints:
      compact: 520px
      navigation: 640px
      toolbar: 760px
    strategy: "Break at content failure points; keep the body free of horizontal scrolling."

constraints:
  always:
    - Use semantic `--dm-*` variables for color and reusable visual decisions.
    - Keep light, explicit dark, and system dark themes legible and synchronized.
    - Keep one filled primary action per view or dialog.
    - Provide default, hover, focus-visible, active, disabled, loading, empty, and error states where applicable.
    - Use the 4px spacing scale and four-pixel semantic radius unless content geometry requires an explicitly documented exception.
    - Keep data and user-provided identifiers truncatable only when the full value remains available through title, tooltip, or detail view.
    - Use tabular numerals for dynamic counts and numeric columns.
    - Keep overlay and route motion under 300ms and provide reduced-motion behavior.
  never:
    - Add raw palette values to page CSS or JavaScript when a semantic color token exists.
    - Introduce a second component framework or parallel token namespace.
    - Use Folder Gold as a decorative wash across multiple competing regions.
    - Show more than one filled primary action in the same view or dialog.
    - Use `transition: all`, unbounded z-index values, or layout-property animation.
    - Remove focus outlines without an equal or stronger focus-visible replacement.
    - Use hover as the only way to discover or invoke a core action.
    - Change font weight between interaction states.
    - Put persistent page content in an overlay when it belongs in the normal information hierarchy.

rationale:
  colors: |
    The palette is intentionally warm rather than neutral-grey. Parchment canvas
    and ivory surfaces establish the archive/workbench character; umber text
    keeps contrast grounded. Folder Gold carries identity, primary action, and
    selection. Status hues are separate so gold never ambiguously means success
    or warning. Dark mode remaps the same roles onto charcoal-brown layers rather
    than inverting light colors.
  typography: |
    Bahnschrift/DIN-style display faces give headings the labeled, engineered
    character of folders and utility hardware. Segoe/PingFang keeps dense Chinese
    application text familiar and readable. Cascadia/SFMono is reserved for IDs,
    code, timestamps, and machine-shaped data.
  layout: |
    This is an operational desktop application, so density and stable regions
    matter more than editorial whitespace. Toolbars expose current context and
    one primary action. Lists and tables own their scrolling, while responsive
    breakpoints stack filters and navigation only when content fails to fit.
  elevation: |
    Borders perform most separation. Small warm shadows lift cards gently;
    stronger layered shadows are reserved for dialogs, popovers, and drawers.
    Dark mode deepens shadow opacity while keeping borders visible.
  shapes: |
    Four-pixel semantic corners are the defining geometry for controls, cards,
    badges, avatars, and overlays. Larger radii exist for exceptional branded or
    media treatments but should not soften ordinary application chrome.
  motion: |
    Fast 120–240ms motion communicates route direction, overlay presence, and
    control response. It is functional and infrequent, uses transform/opacity
    where practical, and yields to reduced-motion preferences.
  dos:
    - Let warm neutral layers and crisp hierarchy carry the interface.
    - Reserve Folder Gold for primary action and current selection.
    - Prefer separators over shadows in dense record collections.
    - Preserve concrete Chinese task language and established technical terms.
  donts:
    - Do not turn the archival reference into skeuomorphic paper textures.
    - Do not scatter gradients, glows, or gold accents as decoration.
    - Do not replace compact controls with oversized marketing-page proportions.
    - Do not introduce cool generic grey palettes that erase the Folder Gold identity.

sources:
  - path: frontend/src/dmui.css
    role: "Normative CSS token declarations, light/dark mappings, DMUI components, state variants, motion, responsive behavior, and utilities."
    inspected_at: 2026-09-12
  - path: frontend/src/style.css
    role: "Shared application page composition, content toolbars, filters, route states, responsive layouts, and application-level motion."
    inspected_at: 2026-09-12
  - path: frontend/src/pages/automation.css
    role: "Adjacent master-detail workflow showing how the shared system is consumed by the automation workspace."
    inspected_at: 2026-09-12

